(6431687, 953132, 130301, '<td valign="top">"but to realistically portray an image of killing someone....goes over the top for me."  Are you serious?  Does this mean you never watch horror movies, or movies that realisticly portray violence.  Many top Academy Award winning movies have realistic images of death and violence.  Anyone would know that its FAKE, an image, fantasy...whatever you want to call it.  Disturbing , maybe, but not real!  If this website were full of nothing but images of pretty sunsets, and flowers, Iprobably wouldn''t be a part of it.  Because it would be BORING!</td>', '"but to realistically portray an image of killing someone....goes over the top for me."  Are you serious?  Does this mean you never watch horror movies, or movies that realisticly portray violence.  Many top Academy Award winning movies have realistic images of death and violence.  Anyone would know that its FAKE, an image, fantasy...whatever you want to call it.  Disturbing , maybe, but not real!  If this website were full of nothing but images of pretty sunsets, and flowers, Iprobably wouldn''t be a part of it.  Because it would be BORING!', '2011-06-02 09:43:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6431797, 953197, 76712, '<td valign="top">You made front page of 1x!!!!!!<br/> <br/>AHHHH WELL DONE!</td>', 'You made front page of 1x!!!!!! AHHHH WELL DONE!', '2011-06-02 11:56:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6431854, 953197, 63503, '<td valign="top">I wonder why you did not complete the effect by placing a 5th Speedlight inside the fridge''s real light fixture. As it is now it looks obviously in the ''off'' state. I am surprised you omitted this since you could have easily accomplished the task by disassembling the fridge to uncover the guts of the fixture, changing the fixture acrylic diffuser to a larger one to accommodate the Speedlight, rigging a radio trigger inside the roof of the fridge to make sure the Speedlight triggers in sync and then re-assembling the fridge, all of which you could have quickly accomplished in no more than 16 hours of work, not counting the time required for the reverse process to retrieve your Speedlight and the radio trigger after taking the picture. Come on, it is not like you needed to truck the fridge over to a lake and build a special table in the middle of the lake. I am afraid you are beginning to slack. Congratulations on getting the blue despite the blatant omission, but please try harder next time ;-)</td>', 'I wonder why you did not complete the effect by placing a 5th Speedlight inside the fridge''s real light fixture. As it is now it looks obviously in the ''off'' state. I am surprised you omitted this since you could have easily accomplished the task by disassembling the fridge to uncover the guts of the fixture, changing the fixture acrylic diffuser to a larger one to accommodate the Speedlight, rigging a radio trigger inside the roof of the fridge to make sure the Speedlight triggers in sync and then re-assembling the fridge, all of which you could have quickly accomplished in no more than 16 hours of work, not counting the time required for the reverse process to retrieve your Speedlight and the radio trigger after taking the picture. Come on, it is not like you needed to truck the fridge over to a lake and build a special table in the middle of the lake. I am afraid you are beginning to slack. Congratulations on getting the blue despite the blatant omission, but please try harder next time ;-)', '2011-06-02 12:47:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6431943, 953197, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by senor_kasper:</b></div><hr/><i> I wonder why you did not complete the effect by placing a 5th Speedlight inside the fridge''s real light fixture. As it is now it looks obviously in the ''off'' state. I am surprised you omitted this since you could have easily accomplished the task by disassembling the fridge to uncover the guts of the fixture, changing the fixture acrylic diffuser to a larger one to accommodate the Speedlight, rigging a radio trigger inside the roof of the fridge to make sure the Speedlight triggers in sync and then re-assembling the fridge, all of which you could have quickly accomplished in no more than 16 hours of work, not counting the time required for the reverse process to retrieve your Speedlight and the radio trigger after taking the picture. Come on, it is not like you needed to truck the fridge over to a lake and build a special table in the middle of the lake. I am afraid you are beginning to slack. Congratulations on getting the blue despite the blatant omission, but please try harder next time ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are so right about that. The true reason for this slack is kinda sad: I don''t have the money for a 5th Speedlight. So as I am writing this, I am training a dozen of glowworms to deliver a burst of light on demand, but my cats are eating them regularly, so it is not THAT easy.</td>', 'Originally posted by senor_kasper: I wonder why you did not complete the effect by placing a 5th Speedlight inside the fridge''s real light fixture. As it is now it looks obviously in the ''off'' state. I am surprised you omitted this since you could have easily accomplished the task by disassembling the fridge to uncover the guts of the fixture, changing the fixture acrylic diffuser to a larger one to accommodate the Speedlight, rigging a radio trigger inside the roof of the fridge to make sure the Speedlight triggers in sync and then re-assembling the fridge, all of which you could have quickly accomplished in no more than 16 hours of work, not counting the time required for the reverse process to retrieve your Speedlight and the radio trigger after taking the picture. Come on, it is not like you needed to truck the fridge over to a lake and build a special table in the middle of the lake. I am afraid you are beginning to slack. Congratulations on getting the blue despite the blatant omission, but please try harder next time ;-)   You are so right about that. The true reason for this slack is kinda sad: I don''t have the money for a 5th Speedlight. So as I am writing this, I am training a dozen of glowworms to deliver a burst of light on demand, but my cats are eating them regularly, so it is not THAT easy.', '2011-06-02 15:22:23.000000', NULL, 0),
