(6432334, 953197, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by senor_kasper:</b></div><hr/><i> I wonder why you did not complete the effect by placing a 5th Speedlight inside the fridge''s real light fixture. As it is now it looks obviously in the ''off'' state. I am surprised you omitted this since you could have easily accomplished the task by disassembling the fridge to uncover the guts of the fixture, changing the fixture acrylic diffuser to a larger one to accommodate the Speedlight, rigging a radio trigger inside the roof of the fridge to make sure the Speedlight triggers in sync and then re-assembling the fridge, all of which you could have quickly accomplished in no more than 16 hours of work, not counting the time required for the reverse process to retrieve your Speedlight and the radio trigger after taking the picture. Come on, it is not like you needed to truck the fridge over to a lake and build a special table in the middle of the lake. I am afraid you are beginning to slack. Congratulations on getting the blue despite the blatant omission, but please try harder next time ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are so right about that. The true reason for this slack is kinda sad: I don''t have the money for a 5th Speedlight. So as I am writing this, I am training a dozen of glowworms to deliver a burst of light on demand, but my cats are eating them regularly, so it is not THAT easy. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It seems like you could have come up with something, Christophe. The problem with you, is that you just don''t go that extra mile for a shot! :P<br/> <br/>Congrats! Your wife did an excellent job. It looks just like you! :D</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Originally posted by senor_kasper: I wonder why you did not complete the effect by placing a 5th Speedlight inside the fridge''s real light fixture. As it is now it looks obviously in the ''off'' state. I am surprised you omitted this since you could have easily accomplished the task by disassembling the fridge to uncover the guts of the fixture, changing the fixture acrylic diffuser to a larger one to accommodate the Speedlight, rigging a radio trigger inside the roof of the fridge to make sure the Speedlight triggers in sync and then re-assembling the fridge, all of which you could have quickly accomplished in no more than 16 hours of work, not counting the time required for the reverse process to retrieve your Speedlight and the radio trigger after taking the picture. Come on, it is not like you needed to truck the fridge over to a lake and build a special table in the middle of the lake. I am afraid you are beginning to slack. Congratulations on getting the blue despite the blatant omission, but please try harder next time ;-)   You are so right about that. The true reason for this slack is kinda sad: I don''t have the money for a 5th Speedlight. So as I am writing this, I am training a dozen of glowworms to deliver a burst of light on demand, but my cats are eating them regularly, so it is not THAT easy.   It seems like you could have come up with something, Christophe. The problem with you, is that you just don''t go that extra mile for a shot! :P Congrats! Your wife did an excellent job. It looks just like you! :D', '2011-06-02 23:20:49.000000', NULL, 0),
